e="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1045_765697_1502853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text displayed by Web browsers during image downloads for users who have graphics turned off, and for users who rely on screen-reading software to convert graphics on the screen to spoken words.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="765697">ALT text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1502853">ALT текст</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10450_102839_1503902"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To put new data in the place of other data, usually after conducting a search for the data to be replaced. Text-based applications such as word processors typically include Find and Replace commands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="102839">replace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1503902">замијенити</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10451_16349_1503903"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Relating to frequencies within the range of perception by the human ear - from about 15 to 20,000 hertz (cycles per second).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16349">audio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1503903">аудио</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10452_107217_2541543"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In color management, the purity of a color's hue, moving from gray to the pure color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="107217">saturation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2541543">засићење</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10459_116136_2120242"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of markup in markup languages. A start tag is the starting element of a tag pair which contains metainformation about some part of the text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116136">start tag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2120242">почетна ознака</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammatic