</termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10657_307433_406551"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The prefix that is used to direct a call internationally. The International Access Code is 011 in the United States and 00 in much of the rest of the world.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307433">international access code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="406551">међународни префикс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10678_103034_1725713"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application, commonly part of a database management program, that uses a report form created by the user to lay out and print the contents of a database. A report generator is used to select specific record fields or ranges of records, to make the output attractive by including such features as headings, running heads, page numbers, and fonts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="103034">report generator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1725713">генератор извештаја</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10678_103035_1725713"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application, commonly part of a database management program, 