ular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15279_19094_1504383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to separate directory names in MS-DOS and UNIX path specifications. When used as a leading character, it means that the path specification begins from the topmost level for that disk drive.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="19094">backslash</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1504383">обрнута коса црта</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15279_318431_1504383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to separate directory names in MS-DOS and UNIX path specifications. When used as a leading character, it means that the path specification begins from the topmost level for that disk drive.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318431">REVERSE SOLIDUS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1504383">обрнута коса црта</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15279_318714_1504383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to separate directory names in MS-DOS and UNIX path specifications. When used as a leading character, it means that the path specification begins f