ereby altered or obliterated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="40131">corruption</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2701447">оштећење</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1565_116540_1502911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To halt a process or action, typically without restoring the prior state.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116540">stop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1502911">стати</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15677_147745_1504424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The order in which changes are propagated from replica to replica. Topology determines how quickly changes in another replica appear in your replica.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147745">replica set topology</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1504424">топологија</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15677_359275_1504424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The order in which changes are propagated from replica to replica. Topology determines how quickly changes in another replica appear in your replica.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="359275">topology</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1504424">топологија</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15680_380755_1788788"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user that performs a service, or the equipment or facility that is required for a service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="380755">resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1788788">ресурс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15684_35399_1504425"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An instruction to a computer program that, when issued by the user, causes an action to be carried out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="35399">command</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1504425">команда</term