 enter information for the methods by which they can be contacted, such as Messenger, home phone, mobile phone, and email.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217817">Contact info</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218149">контакт информације</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25825_1217869_1917159"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option that enables the user to see the different parts of a nested formula evaluated in the order the formula is calculated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217869">Evaluate Formula</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1917159">Анализирај формулу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25825_1217869_2528072"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option that enables the user to see the different parts of a nested formula evaluated in the order the formula is calculated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217869">Evaluate Formula</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528072">Провера формуле</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2583_335548_2542075"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option, found on the Business Contact Manager menu, that enables the user to customize multiple fields.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="335548">Manage User-Defined Fields</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2542075">Управљање кориснички дефинисаним пољима</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25837_1217966_1778359"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Outlook Live feature in the Web management interface that enables migration of the contents of user mailboxes from an on-premises IMAP messaging system to Outlook Live (or Exchange Online).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1217966">Email Migration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778359">Миграција е-поште</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2584_235070_1503018"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo organizer used to view, manage, and edit digital pictures.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235070">Windows Photo Gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1503018">Windows фотогалерија</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2584_725946_1503018"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo organizer used to view, manage, and edit digital pictures.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="725946">Photo Gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1503018">Windows фотогалерија</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25844_1218374_1778499"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The domain name of the Outlook Live domain that you are configuring with Outlook Live Directory Sync (OLSync)(previously known as GALSync 2010). When you deploy OLSync, you manually enter at least one provisioning domain, for example, student.contoso.edu, during the ILM 2007 configuration process. The provisioning domain must be an accepted domain in your Outlook Live deployment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218374">provisioning domain</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778499">иницијални домен</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25845_1218375_1778253"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A domain or a person that an end user doesn't want to receive email messages from. Messages received from any email address or domain listed in the users' Blocked Senders list are sent directly to the user's Junk E-Mail folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218375">blocked sender</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778253">блокирани пошиљалац</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25846_1218376_1778440"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Active Directory security principal object that has at least one associated SMTP address</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218376">mail-enabled user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778440">корисник поште</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25847_1218377_1778404"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The administrator user interface in Outlook Live used to import new users with a CSV file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218377">Import users</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778404">Увоз корисника</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25848_1218378_1778296"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A comma separated value (CSV) file used to provision many new users at one time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218378">CSV import file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778296">CSV датотека увоза</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25849_1218379_1778403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of provisioning new users using a CSV file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218379">import process</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778403">процес увоза</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25850_1218380_1778592"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The administrative boundary in which members of an Exchange 2010 role group can make changes. For the Outlook Live hosted service, the write scope is the entire Outlook Live organization. For on-premises implementations of Microsoft Exchange Server 2010, write scopes may be smaller in breadth, such as those defined by a specific organizational unit or a database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218380">write scope</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778592">опсег уписивања</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25851_1218381_1778334"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The role group that gives users the permissions needed to use Multi-Mailbox Search.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218381">Discovery Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778334">Управљање откривањем</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25852_1218382_1778390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The role group that gives users the permissions to reset passwords for users and manage settings on the Options page for users' Outlook Live account. To help troubleshoot user issues, members can also view, but not modify, all mailboxes, public groups, and external contacts in the organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218382">Help Desk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778390">Техничка подршка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25853_1218383_1778503"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The role group that gives users the permissions to create and manage mailboxes, public groups, and external contacts. Members can also import new users, track messages sent and received by users, and manage Exchange ActiveSync settings for the organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218383">Recipient Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778503">Управљање примаоцима</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25854_1218384_1778505"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The role group that gives users permissions to create and manage organization-wide rules, also known as transport rules. Members of the role group can also track messages sent and received by users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218384">Records Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778505">Управљање записима</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25855_1218385_1778572"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The role group that gives users the permissions to manage Unified Messaging (UM) server configurations, UM properties on mailboxes, UM prompts, and UM auto attendant configuration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218385">UM Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778572">Управљање обједињеном разменом порука</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25856_1218386_1778579"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The administrator role group that gives users permissions to view, but not modify, all mailboxes, public groups, and external contacts in the organization. Members can also view settings for role assignment policies, transport rules, and supervision policies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218386">View-Only Organization Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778579">Управљање организацијом само са приказом</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25857_1218387_1652555"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A domain or a person that a user wants to always receive email messages from. Users add recipients and domains to the Safe Senders list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218387">safe sender</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1652555">сигурни пошиљалац</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25857_1218387_1778522"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A domain or a person that a user wants to always receive email messages from. Users add recipients and domains to the Safe Senders list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218387">safe sender</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778522">безбедан пошиљалац</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25857_1218387_2795076"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A domain or a person that a user wants to always receive email messages from. Users add recipients and domains to the Safe Senders list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218387">safe sender</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795076">безбједан пошиљалац</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25858_1218388_1778460"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature in Exchange 2010 and Outlook Live that enables users to search the mailboxes in their organization for email and other message types that contain specific keywords. The results of a search are then copied to a mailbox that you have specified so that you can review, organize, and export the search results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218388">Multi-Mailbox Search</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778460">Претраживање више поштанских сандучића</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25859_1218389_1778575"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An item that can't be indexed for a mailbox search using Multi-Mailbox Search. This includes unrecognized message types and messages that contain attachments that are encrypted or have an unrecognized format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218389">unsearchable item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778575">ставка која се не може претраживати</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25860_1218390_1778382"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who is assigned the ability to approve and reject any messages sent to a public group or a dynamic distribution group.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1218390">group moderator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778382">модератор групе</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25862_1223075_1778520"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of resource mailbox that is assigned to a meeting location such as a conference room, auditorium, or training room. Room mailboxes can be included as resources in meeting requests, providing a simple and efficient way of organizing meetings for an organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1223075">room mailbox</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778520">поштанско сандуче собе</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25865_1223099_2729533"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A notice sent to employees of an organization instructing them to preserve all documents that may be relevant to a legal case.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1223099">legal hold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2729533">правна задршка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25865_1223099_2729538"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A notice sent to employees of an organization instructing them to preserve all documents that may be relevant to a legal case.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1223099">legal hold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2729538">задршка за потребе судског спора</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="25865_2726542_2729533"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A notice sent to employees of an organization instructing them to preserve all documents that may be relevant to a legal case.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><ter