_1644567"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that audibly reads the text on the screen aloud and describes some events to users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1608135">Narrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1644567">Наратор</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="316_137462_2527477"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A machine-wide code cache used for side-by-side storage of assemblies. There are two parts to the cache: the global assembly cache contains assemblies that are explicitly installed to be shared among many applications on the computer; the download cache stores code downloaded from Internet or intranet sites, isolated to the application that triggered the download so that code downloaded on behalf of one application/page does not impact other applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="137462">assembly cache</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2527477">кеш склопа</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31621_1608186_1675728"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables single-click access to trend and contribution patterns within a PivotTable or 