 type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46353_2612185_2612469"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The consumer-friendly name for virtualization-based security (VBS). The VBS service in Windows 10 uses hardware virtualization features to create and isolate a secure region of memory from the normal operating system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612185">Core isolation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612469">Изолација језгра</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46354_2612186_2612470"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of open tabs, including applications, files, pages, or websites, which can be saved together and re-opened together when you want to continue with that set of tabs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612186">set</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612470">скуп</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46375_2612854_2616412"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A date when Microsoft will no longer provide updates to a feature release of a product, such that a customer needs to upgrade to a new feature release to continue receiving support from Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2612854">end of service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2616412">престанак пружања услуге</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46375_2878237_2616412"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A date when Microsoft will no longer provide updates to a feature release of a product, such that a customer needs to upgrade to a new feature release to continue receiving support from Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2878237">EOL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2616412">престанак пружања услуге</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="46381_3128246_3128823"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature for Windows commercial customers that helps mitigate security threats by restricting the applications that users are allowed to run and the code that runs in the System Core (kernel).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3128246">App Control for Business</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">No