ype="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2891762">Дан државности</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51301_2891089_2892125"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Slovenian national holiday celebrated on June 25 to commemorate Slovenia's declaration of independence from Yugoslavia in 1991.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2891089">Statehood Day</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2892125">Дан државности</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51302_2891211_2891764"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The national holiday in Bosnia and Herzegovina celebrated on November 25 to commemorate the day in 1943 on which ZAVNOBiH, the Anti-Fascist Council of Bosnia and Herzegovina, adopted a resolution to declare the country/region an equal community of Muslims, Serbs, and Croats.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2891211">Statehood Day (Bosnia and Herzegovina)</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2891764">Дан државности (Босна и Херцеговина)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</te