 quantifiable measurement, such as monthly gross profit or quarterly employee turnover, used to monitor an organization's performance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2955560">CUBEKPIMEMBER</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2978825">CUBEKPIMEMBER</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52349_2955561_2978826"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Cube Excel function that returns a member or tuple in a cube hierarchy. Use to validate that the member or tuple exists in the cube.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2955561">CUBEMEMBER</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2978826">CUBEMEMBER</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52350_2955562_2978827"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Cube Excel function that returns the value of a member property in the cube. Use to validate that a member name exists within the cube and to return the specified property for this member.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2955562">CUBEMEMBERPROPERTY</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2978827">CUBEMEMBERPROPERTY</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52351_2955563_2978828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Cube Excel function that returns the nth, or ranked, member in a set. Use to return one or more elements in a set, such as the top sales performer or top 10 students.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2955563">CUBERANKEDMEMBER</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2978828">CUBERANKEDMEMBER</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52352_2955564_2978829"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Cube Excel function that defines a calculated set of members or tuples by sending a set expression to the cube on the server, which creates the set, and then returns that set to Microsoft Office Excel.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2955564">CUBESET</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sr-Cyrl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2978829">CUBESET</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">SRB, BIH</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></ter